# THEOPHYSICS HUB — DEPLOYMENT GUIDE
## POF 2828 · Unified System Architecture
### Version 1.0 · March 10, 2026

---

## WHAT THIS DOCUMENT IS

This is the complete build specification for the Theophysics Hub — a unified system that starts as standalone HTML tools on a Windows desktop and scales into a full Cloudflare-hosted PWA with AI agents that learn, organize, and build on David's research.

Any AI reading this document should be able to execute every phase without additional context.

---

## SYSTEM OVERVIEW

The Theophysics Hub is a three-phase deployment:

**Phase 1 — Local Tools (Sealed HTML):** Three standalone HTML files that run from Windows Startup with zero dependencies. localStorage only. No server, no build step, no framework.

**Phase 2 — Local Hub + Notes:** A launcher page that unifies all tools into a tabbed dashboard with a built-in notes/scratch system. Still pure HTML. Still runs from a local folder.

**Phase 3 — Cloudflare PWA + AI:** Deploy to Cloudflare Pages. Add manifest.json and service worker. Connect to existing Cloudflare Workers via a gateway. AI agents on Cloudflare get access to R2 buckets, D1 databases, and all user data. The system becomes self-improving.

---

## PHASE 1: SEALED HTML TOOLS

### Design Principles
- Single HTML file per tool. No external dependencies except Google Fonts.
- localStorage is the ONLY data store.
- Export/Import via JSON for backup and portability.
- Every tool must work by double-clicking the HTML file. No server.
- All tools share the same brand system (see Brand Spec below).
- Each tool has a dual-mode API layer: a single variable (`GATEWAY_URL`) that, when set, enables Cloudflare sync on top of localStorage. Default is `null` (offline only).

### Tool 1: Clipboard Manager (COMPLETE)
- **File:** `clipboard.html`
- **Location:** `C:\Users\lowes\AppData\Roaming\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs\Startup\`
- **Features:**
  - Two-pane layout: card list (left) + detail view (right)
  - 20 hotkey slots: Ctrl+Shift+1-9 (slots 1-9), Ctrl+Shift+0 (slot 10), Ctrl+Shift+F1-F10 (slots 11-20)
  - Ctrl+Shift+V: instant capture from system clipboard
  - Ctrl+Shift+N: new clip
  - Arrow keys + Enter: navigate and copy
  - Pin, tag, search, filter (All / Pinned / Tagged / Hotkeyed)
  - Export/Import JSON
  - localStorage key: `pof2828_clips`

### Tool 2: Prompt Picker (TO BUILD)
- **File:** `prompt_picker.html`
- **Features:**
  - Two-pane layout: prompt list with category tabs (left) + full prompt view with copy/edit/use actions (right)
  - Categories as horizontal tabs (All, Framework, Research, Meta, Custom...)
  - Each prompt card shows: Title, one-line purpose, tags, hotkey badge if assigned
  - Prominent green "Copy" button on every card (consistent with clipboard design)
  - Create/Edit modal: name, category, content (textarea), hotkey (AHK format), tags
  - Hotkey display: show as human-readable (Ctrl+Shift+1 not ^+1)
  - Search across name, content, and tags
  - Export/Import JSON
  - localStorage key: `pof2828_prompts`
- **Data Shape:**
```json
{
  "id": "p_abc123",
  "name": "Deep Laws Extraction",
  "category": "Framework",
  "content": "Run /DEEPER then /INTEGRATE on this passage...",
  "hotkey": "^+1",
  "tags": ["framework", "extraction", "deeper"],
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T12:00:00Z"
}
```

### Tool 3: Research Links (TO BUILD)
- **File:** `research_links.html`
- **Features:**
  - Two-pane layout: bookmark list with category tabs (left) + link detail with preview/notes (right)
  - Categories: Theophysics, Infrastructure, Research, Consciousness, Physics, General
  - Color-coded cards by category (gold, blue, green, purple, cyan, gray)
  - Each card: Title, URL (truncated), tags, action row (Open, Copy URL, Edit, Delete)
  - "Open" button launches URL in new tab
  - Notes field per bookmark (for personal annotations)
  - Search across title, URL, tags, and notes
  - Export/Import JSON
  - localStorage key: `pof2828_bookmarks`
- **Data Shape:**
```json
{
  "id": "b_xyz789",
  "title": "Global Consciousness Project",
  "url": "https://noosphere.princeton.edu",
  "category": "Consciousness",
  "tags": ["gcp", "coherence", "6sigma"],
  "notes": "325+ replicas, 6sigma through 2010. Key evidence for global psi-field.",
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T12:00:00Z"
}
```

### Tool 4: Notes / Scratch Pad (TO BUILD)
- **File:** `notes.html`
- **Features:**
  - Two-pane: note list (left) + editor (right)
  - Markdown-aware textarea with preview toggle
  - Auto-save to localStorage on every keystroke (debounced 500ms)
  - Tags, pinning, search
  - "Send to Clipboard" button (copies content, also stores in clipboard localStorage if same browser)
  - Timestamp tracking (created, last modified)
  - Export individual note as .md or all notes as JSON
  - localStorage key: `pof2828_notes`
- **Data Shape:**
```json
{
  "id": "n_def456",
  "title": "Auto-generated from first line",
  "content": "Full markdown content...",
  "tags": ["trinity", "proof"],
  "pinned": false,
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T12:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-10T14:30:00Z"
}
```

